  "body": "### Summary\n\nCapture on the Mac, with the LOT-001 (#38) kit (`tooling/fixtures/`), the page state: Topic page with `quote_only=1` (LOT-001 (#38) checklist R34, dropped as optional): is there any server signal that someone quoted me?\n\n### Scope\n\nState to capture: Topic page with `quote_only=1` (LOT-001 (#38) checklist R34, dropped as optional): is there any server signal that someone quoted me?\n\nNote: read-only GET; settles feasibility before FEAT-018 (#162) is promised\n\nRules: anonymize every free-text field; never hand-build the state in the cloud (LESSONS 36); add a legacy oracle when a parser consumes it (LOT-002 (#39)..005 tooling); one PR per batch of captures; the PR removes the row from the Capture backlog.\n\n### Wanted by\n\nFEAT-018 (#162), HFR-PROTOCOL §7b B11\n\n### Depends on\n\n—\n\n### Owner / session\n\n— (ready; `host: mac`)\n\n### Source\n\n`docs/LOTS.md` \"Capture backlog (Mac)\", copied from the frozen old issue [francoisgn/ios-app_SwiftHFR#98](https://github.com/francoisgn/ios-app_SwiftHFR/issues/98).\n",
